From f6286df8c2f696d2cc64579a88bc85042baa0cad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:52:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Accessibility POC: speak the help title under the mouse
 (--access)

Phase 0 of doc/@AI_Plans/PRD-Accessibility.md. Additive and off by default;
no original game function is edited.

- platform/include/Platform_Speech.h, platform/speech/PFL_Speech.c:
  Platform_Speak() for every backend. Windows loads Tolk.dll at runtime
  (NVDA, JAWS, ... with SAPI fallback); Linux runs spd-say; macOS runs say;
  Platform_Headless is log-only so tests can assert on what would be spoken.
- MoX/src/Access.c: when the pointer enters a different right-click-help
  area, speak that HELP.LBX record's title. Reads HELP.LBX itself rather than
  through LBX_Load_Data_Static(), which shares a cached handle and is fatal
  on error.
- src/ReMoM.c: --access / REMOM_ACCESS=1 enables it and registers
  Access_Frame as the frame callback (unless --scenario already owns it).
- MoX/tests/test_Access.cpp: 7 tests against a synthetic HELP.LBX.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
